  "preview": "Mount Kilimanjaro tops out at 5,895 m above sea level. The Java Trench bottoms at 7,290 m below. How far apart are they — and where is the midpoint?",
  "body": {
    "goal": "Use signed numbers to compute differences and midpoints across sea level, distinguishing magnitude from direction, and to estimate strategically before computing.",
    "studentPrompt": "Mount Kilimanjaro is the highest point in Africa. Its peak is 5,895 meters above sea level.\n\nThe Java Trench is in the Indian Ocean, off the coast of Indonesia. Its lowest point is 7,290 meters below sea level.\n\n1. What is the total vertical distance from the bottom of the Java Trench to the peak of Kilimanjaro?\n2. Is the elevation halfway between these two points above or below sea level? Decide *without* doing the full calculation. Explain how you know.\n3. What is the elevation of the exact midpoint?\n4. A submarine sits at -2,500 m. Which is closer — the surface, the trench bottom, or the peak of Kilimanjaro?",
    "image": {
      "alt": "A side-view scene with a snow-capped Mt. Kilimanjaro silhouette on the left under a pale sky, and a deep ocean on the right with a small submarine descending toward the dark Java Trench.",
      "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 480 220\" font-family=\"system-ui, sans-serif\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"sky\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"1\"><stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#fde8c8\"/><stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#cfe6f2\"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id=\"sea\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"1\"><stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#3a7ca5\"/><stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#0b2747\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"480\" height=\"110\" fill=\"url(#sky)\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"110\" width=\"480\" height=\"110\" fill=\"url(#sea)\"/><circle cx=\"380\" cy=\"40\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#fff3b0\" opacity=\"0.85\"/><polygon points=\"40,110 130,110 95,55\" fill=\"#7a8a73\" opacity=\"0.55\"/><polygon points=\"60,110 220,110 150,30\" fill=\"#5b6b56\"/><polygon points=\"130,75 150,30 175,70 162,72 155,60 145,72\" fill=\"#f7fafc\"/><polygon points=\"95,90 110,70 122,88\" fill=\"#f7fafc\" opacity=\"0.85\"/><path d=\"M0,112 Q40,108 80,112 T160,112 T240,112 T320,112 T400,112 T480,112\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#bfe3f0\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" opacity=\"0.7\"/><path d=\"M260,210 Q330,150 400,200 Q440,215 470,205 L470,220 L260,220 Z\" fill=\"#06182f\"/><g transform=\"translate(330,160)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"18\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#e2c044\"/><circle cx=\"7\" cy=\"-1\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#bfe3f0\"/><rect x=\"-6\" y=\"-11\" width=\"10\" height=\"5\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#e2c044\"/><line x1=\"-18\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-23\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#e2c044\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"-25\" cy=\"0\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#fff3b0\" opacity=\"0.8\"/></g><g fill=\"#bfe3f0\" opacity=\"0.85\"><path d=\"M280,135 q3,-3 6,0 q-3,1 -6,0 z\"/><path d=\"M285,135 l5,-2 -5,-2 z\"/></g><g fill=\"#bfe3f0\" opacity=\"0.7\"><path d=\"M420,150 q3,-3 6,0 q-3,1 -6,0 z\"/><path d=\"M425,150 l5,-2 -5,-2 z\"/></g><text x=\"150\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1f2a44\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\">Mt. Kilimanjaro</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#cfe6f2\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\">Java Trench</text></svg>"
    },
    "launch": "Tell the story. Show students a globe (or just point at where Africa and Indonesia are). Ask: 'If you went from the bottom of the Java Trench to the top of Kilimanjaro, how far up would you go?' Send them to the boards.",
    "materials": [
      "Vertical whiteboards",
      "Markers",
      "Optional: globe or world map"
    ],
    "concepts": [
      "signed-numbers",
      "subtraction",
      "absolute-value",
      "midpoint",
      "real-world-application"
    ],
    "taskType": "investigation",
    "btcFit": "Solid BTC task. Low floor (anyone can compute one of the parts), the midpoint reasoning in Q2 is the diamond. Q4 surprises kids who haven't thought about asymmetric magnitude.",
    "anticipatedApproaches": "- Q1: Some groups add 5895 + 7290 = 13,185 m. Others compute 5895 - (-7290) and arrive at the same answer. Both are right.\n- Q2: Strong groups reason 'the trench is deeper than the mountain is tall, so the midpoint is below sea level.' Weaker groups jump to calculation without the reasoning.\n- Q3: Midpoint = (5895 + (-7290)) / 2 = -1395 / 2 = -697.5 m. About 700 m below sea level.\n- Q4: Submarine is at -2500. Distances: to surface = 2500, to trench = 4790, to peak = 8395. Surface is closest.",
    "commonMisconceptions": "- Subtracting magnitudes without considering signs (5895 - 7290 = -1395 — close, but missing the geometric meaning).\n- Saying the midpoint is at sea level because '+5895 and -7290 cancel to about zero' (they don't — they sum to negative).\n- For Q4, computing 5895 - 2500 = 3395 to get 'distance to peak' (forgetting the submarine is BELOW sea level, so the distance to the peak is 5895 + 2500).",
    "discussionQuestions": "- Two groups got the same answer to Q1 by different methods (one added, one subtracted with negatives). Why do they agree?\n- In Q2, what reasoning told you the midpoint was below sea level *before* you computed?\n- For Q4, the surface is the closest answer, even though it's the same direction as the trench. Does that make sense? Why?",
    "extensions": "- Mount Everest is 8,849 m. The Mariana Trench is -10,994 m (Challenger Deep). Repeat the four questions with this pair. Is the midpoint above or below sea level? By how much?\n- A scuba diver descends from the surface at a steady -2 m/s. After how long is she at -100 m? Now relate this rate to a hot-air balloon rising at +3 m/s from sea level. When are they at the same elevation? When is the absolute distance between them smallest?",
    "sampleSolutions": "1. Distance = 5895 - (-7290) = 5895 + 7290 = 13,185 m total vertical span.\n2. Below sea level. Reason: |-7290| > |5895|, so the trench dominates — the midpoint will fall on the trench side.\n3. Midpoint = (5895 + (-7290)) / 2 = -1395 / 2 = -697.5 m. About 698 m below sea level.\n4. Submarine at -2500 m. To surface: 2500 m. To trench: |-2500 - (-7290)| = 4790 m. To peak: |5895 - (-2500)| = 8395 m. Surface is closest by about 2300 m over the trench.",
